Skill	craft:github
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; cat $D/take-in.md; ls $D $D/scripts
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; cat $D/tracker.md; echo ----; git remote -v; bash $D/scripts/take-in-check.sh 91
Bash	gh issue view 91 --json title,body
text	**#91 README: the install command says npm instal**  The README tells the reader to run `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so the command fails. The work is done when the README says `npm install shop`.  The take-in check did not clear the issue. It printed:  ``` #91: assigned to you #91: label in progress #91: branch fix/91-typo, 0 commits ahead of main, last commit 2026-11-03T00:00:00Z ```  The issue is already assigned to you and has the label `in progress`. It also has the branch `fix/91-typo`, with no commits past `main`. The check printed no `continue` line, so this computer does not show the work as running here. Another session of yours, on this computer or another one, may already be on it.  **Is the work running somewhere else, or should I continue it here?** If it runs somewhere else, I stop. If here, I take the next steps: the tracker check, the worktree on `fix/91-typo`, the fix, the review and the pull request.
person	It continues here.
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; gh label list 2>&1 | head; git branch -a; bash $D/scripts/collect.sh take-in 91 bug,debt README.md "npm instal" install
Bash	cat <tmp>/collect.IS8lNr; gh issue develop --list 91
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; bash $D/scripts/worktree.sh 91 docs/91-fix-install-command; echo "exit $?"
text	I stopped before making the worktree. Nothing is assigned or created.  **The branch from the check is not in this repository.** This checkout is `acme/shop`. The only branch linked to #91 README: the install command says npm instal is in a different repository, probably a fork:  https://github.com/lee/shop/tree/fix/91-typo  `worktree.sh` stops in this case. If it made a branch here, `gh` would give it the same name as the fork's branch, and the two would be confused. The fork's branch has 0 commits past `main`, so no work on the fix has started there.  The tracker check found no duplicates, no neighbour issues and no open bug or debt issues on the README.  **How should I go on?**  1. **Start fresh here.** I make the branch `docs/91-fix-install-command` in `acme/shop`, link it to #91 and do the fix. The fork's branch stays as it is. 2. **Work on the fork's branch.** I need write access to `lee/shop` for this. Also, `lee` may be someone else, and then the branch is theirs. 3. **Wait.** If `lee` is someone else who is doing the work, I stop here.
